WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.966
This is a baby back tooth in a child's lower jaw. Under it,

00:00:03.966 --> 00:00:05.507
the adult tooth is growing.

00:00:06.307 --> 00:00:09.443
Here, decay has made holes on more than one side of the tooth.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:13.165
A large filling leaves only thin walls of tooth around it.

00:00:13.965 --> 00:00:17.083
For a steel crown, the dentist most often numbs the tooth,

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.341
takes out the decay and trims it a little.

00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:23.469
Then the dentist glues a ready-made metal cap over the whole tooth.

00:00:23.819 --> 00:00:28.023
After 2 years, about 93 in 100 crowns were still working well,

00:00:28.023 --> 00:00:30.667
compared with 80 in 100 large fillings.
